# PR: branch from updated main

When the user asks to create a pull request, always start the branch from the latest `main`:

1. Fetch and update local `main` first (`git fetch origin main` then checkout/pull, or equivalent)
2. Create the new branch from that updated `main` (not from the current feature branch or a stale local `main`)
3. Then apply/commit the work on that branch and open the PR

Do not open a PR from a branch that was created off an outdated `main` without updating first.
